Package: nirs4allformats
Title: Read Near-Infrared Spectroscopy and Spectral File Formats
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Gregory", "Beurier", email = "gregory.beurier@cirad.fr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Thin R binding for the Rust-first 'nirs4all-formats' near-infrared
    spectroscopy (NIRS) file-loading core. When installed via R CMD INSTALL with
    Cargo available, the package compiles a native 'extendr' static library from
    'src/rust/' and dispatches probe, read, and walk calls directly through Rust.
    Without Cargo it falls back to invoking the 'nirs4all-formats' command-line
    interface. This CRAN build ships the core readers (JCAMP-DX, Galactic SPC,
    Bruker OPUS, ASD, ENVI, CSV, Excel, and many vendor ASCII/binary formats).
    The optional large readers (HDF5/netCDF, Parquet/Arrow, MATLAB) are excluded
    to keep the source package within CRAN's size limit; they are available in
    the full build 'nirs4allformats.full' from the R-universe repository (see
    'Additional_repositories') or by building from source with the
    'formats-all' Cargo feature. Feeding an excluded format to this build returns
    an actionable error naming the full package.
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
URL: https://github.com/GBeurier/nirs4all-formats
BugReports: https://github.com/GBeurier/nirs4all-formats/issues
Additional_repositories: https://gbeurier.r-universe.dev
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    jsonlite
